  (inputs.nixpkgs.lib.evalModules {
    modules = [ (inputs.import-tree ./modules) ];
    specialArgs.inputs = inputs;
  }).config.flake;
```

(No `flake-parts` needed; when it's present, flake-parts owns the `flake` option and den's `config.flake` merges into it.)

## 2. `deploy.nodes` via the `flake` output class

`deploy` is a top-level (not per-system) flake attribute, so it uses den's `flake` class: an aspect key named `flake` writes `flake.<attr>` directly. The docs' recommended pattern for a per-host top-level attribute is to build it **in one place from `den.hosts`**, because the `flake` class merges only one level deep — two aspects writing `flake.deploy.nodes.a` and `flake.deploy.nodes.b` would silently clobber each other:

