**The fix** — add the input to your `flake.nix`:

```nix
inputs.den.url = "github:denful/den";
```

and make sure `inputs` actually reaches your modules:
- with **import-tree**: `specialArgs = { inherit inputs; };`
- with **flake-parts**: `inputs.flake-parts.lib.mkFlake { inherit inputs; } (inputs.import-tree ./modules);`

den's own minimal template (`templates/minimal/flake.nix`) is the whole shape in one file:

```nix
{
  outputs =
    inputs:
    (inputs.nixpkgs.lib.evalModules {
      modules = [ (inputs.import-tree ./modules) ];
      specialArgs = { inherit inputs; };
    }).config.flake;

  inputs = {
    nixpkgs.url = "https://channels.nixos.org/nixos-unstable/nixexprs.tar.xz";
    import-tree.url = "github:vic/import-tree";
    den.url = "github:denful/den";
  };
}
```

**How I know:** in `denful/den`, module files like `templates/minimal/modules/den.nix` start with `{ inputs, den, ... }` and do `imports = [ inputs.den.flakeModule ];`. Those `den`/`inputs.den` references only resolve if `den` is one of the flake's declared inputs passed through via `specialArgs`/`mkFlake`. `nix/default.nix` confirms what the den flake exposes (`lib`, `flakeModule`, `flakeOutputs`, `templates`, …), so the reference is to the input named `den`, not an output you need to define yourself.

