function.arguments:
{"answer":"Set your VM-only options under **`virtualisation.vmVariant`** in your configuration. It is a full NixOS module (default `{ }`) that is evaluated as *your* whole module stack plus nixpkgs' `qemu-vm.nix`, and `nixos-rebuild build-vm` builds `system.build.vm`, which is derived from exactly that evaluation:

```nix
{
  # ... your normal options, unchanged ...

  virtualisation.vmVariant = {
    # Regular system options: these only affect the toplevel the VM boots,
    # not the system you build/switch normally.
    boot.kernelParams = [ "console=ttyS0" ];
    services.openssh.enable = true;

    # VM/VM-runner-specific options (declared in qemu-vm.nix):
    virtualisation.memorySize = 2048;
    virtualisation.forwardPorts = [
      { from = "host"; host.port = 8080; guest.port = 80; }
    ];
  };
}
```

Notes:

- `virtualisation.memorySize`, `forwardPorts`, `graphics`, `sharedDirectories`, `qemu.*`, `useNixStoreImage`, `useBootLoader`, etc. only exist *inside* `vmVariant` — setting them at the top level of a normal config is an "option does not exist" error.
- Don't nest `virtualisation.vmVariant` inside itself — nixpkgs throws `virtualisation.vmVariant*.virtualisation.vmVariant is not supported`.
- nixpkgs already handles several VM quirks for you: inside the VM evaluation it overrides `fileSystems`, `swapDevices`, `boot.initrd.luks.devices`, xserver video drivers and wireless with `mkVMOverride` (priority 10, i.e. it beats even `mkForce`). You can opt out of those, e.g. with `virtualisation.fileSystems = lib.mkForce { }` inside `vmVariant`.
- If you use flakes, an alternative (and cleaner when the VM is a distinct deployment) is a second `nixosConfigurations.<name>-vm` entry that imports your common modules plus VM overrides.

How I know: I read this in NixOS/nixpkgs at `nixos-unstable` — `nixos/modules/virtualisation/build-vm.nix` (defines `virtualisation.vmVariant` and sets `system.build.vm = lib.mkDefault config.virtualisation.vmVariant.system.build.vm`; the `vmVariant` module type is `extendModules { modules = [ ./qemu-vm.nix ]; }`), `nixos/modules/virtualisation/qemu-vm.nix` (`system.build.vm` is a `runCommand` that symlinks the extended config's `system.build.toplevel`, and declares the `virtualisation.*` VM options), and `lib/modules.nix` (`mkVMOverride = mkOverride 10`).","confidence":0.85,"gaps":["Did not read the current nixos-rebuild source (nixos-rebuild-ng, pkgs/by-name/ni/nixos-rebuild-ng, rewritten in Python); the claim that build-vm builds system.build.vm rests on nixpkgs' own comment in build-vm.nix, not on nixos-rebuild's code","No eval run: the asker gave no repo/rev to evaluate, and the nixpkgs flake exposes no nixosConfigurations to test vmVariant end-to-end"],"escalate_forced":"no"}

