One caveat, quoted from the noflake template's README: *"Den needs a top-level attribute where to place configurations. For convenience, it is the flake top-level attribute, following the flake outputs schema, even if Den does not need flakes/flake-parts."* So in noflake mode your `default.nix` still produces the `flake.nixosConfigurations.…`-shaped attrset — it's the shape, not the flake machinery.

