{ inputs, ... }: {
  den.aspects.disko.nixos = {
    imports = [ inputs.disko.nixosModules.disko ];
  };
}
```

The NixOS module itself only needs `pkgs`.

**2. `den.batteries.flake-scope` — when the class module itself must declare `inputs`**
Include the battery once, and every class module (NixOS, darwin, home-manager, …) can take `inputs` (plus `den`, `lib`) as a function argument:

```nix
den.default.includes = [ den.batteries.flake-scope ];

den.aspects.tux.homeManager = { inputs, pkgs, ... }: {
  home.packages = [ inputs.my-tool.packages.${pkgs.stdenv.hostPlatform.system}.default ];
};
```

Mechanism (checked in source): `modules/aspects/batteries/flake-scope.nix` resolves `lib`, `inputs`, `den` into the den context (with `collisionPolicy = "class-wins"`), and the class-module wrapper (`nix/lib/aspects/fx/class-module.nix`, `wrapFunctionModule`) inspects `builtins.functionArgs`, pre-applies args present in the context, and advertises only the rest to the module system via `lib.setFunctionArgs` — so a module can take `inputs` exactly like `pkgs`.

**3. flake-parts users: `den.batteries.inputs'`**
Exposes `inputs'` (system already selected) as `_module.args.inputs'` for the host-OS / user / home classes (`modules/aspects/batteries/flake-parts/inputs.nix`):

```nix
den.default.includes = [ den.batteries.inputs' ];
# then: { inputs', pkgs, ... }: { home.packages = [ inputs'.my-tool.packages.default ]; }
```

**4. Home-manager-only values**
Set `home-manager.extraSpecialArgs.<name>` from the host's NixOS config; every user's home modules on that host receive it.

**5. A real `specialArgs` — only for the edge case**
Only when a module must see the value during `imports` resolution (i.e. it has to be a module-system arg before function args exist). Override the host's `instantiate` (default is `inputs.nixpkgs.lib.nixosSystem`; the option's own description in `nix/lib/entities/host.nix` says to set it explicitly for "adding specialArgs when absolutely required"):

```nix
den.hosts.x86_64-linux.myhost = {
  instantiate = args: inputs.nixpkgs.lib.nixosSystem (args // { specialArgs = { inherit inputs; }; });
};
```

Two caveats:
- Flat-form class modules **must** keep `...` in their argument pattern — the module system passes extra args and a missing ellipsis is an eval error. (The only exception: a function whose *only* args are context args, e.g. `{ host }:`, never reaches the module system.)
