```nix
{
  # Only applied when building/running the VM (`nixos-rebuild build-vm`)
  virtualisation.vmVariant = {
    virtualisation.memorySize = 4096;
    virtualisation.graphics = false;
    services.openssh.enable = true;
    networking.firewall.enable = false;
    # ... any other NixOS option, VM-only
  };
}
```

Why this works (from nixpkgs source, `nixos/modules/virtualisation/build-vm.nix`, identical on 23.11/24.11/25.05/master):

- `virtualisation.vmVariant` is an extended-module (default `{}`) whose description is literally: *"Machine configuration to be added for the vm script produced by `nixos-rebuild build-vm`"*.
- `system.build.vm` — the attribute `nixos-rebuild build-vm` builds — is defined as
  `system.build.vm = lib.mkDefault config.virtualisation.vmVariant.system.build.vm;`
  i.e. it's the `system.build.vm` of a *re-evaluation of your whole config* extended with the `virtualisation/qemu-vm.nix` module plus whatever you set in `vmVariant`. Your normal `system.build.toplevel` (what `switch`/`boot` use) is untouched, so these options never leak into the real system.
- `qemu-vm.nix` defines `system.build.vm` as a `run-<system-name>-vm` script (a `runCommand "nixos-vm"` derivation) that boots the config in QEMU.

Notes:

- For `nixos-rebuild build-vm-with-bootloader` there is the sibling option `virtualisation.vmVariantWithBootLoader` (same mechanism, adds `virtualisation.useBootLoader = true`).
- nixpkgs already auto-adjusts a set of options for the VM via `mkVMOverride` inside `qemu-vm.nix` (swap and LUKS disabled, host `fileSystems` replaced by virtiofs/9p mounts, `modesetting` video driver, wireless disabled, `timesyncd` off, ...). If you want to re-enable one of those for the VM only, override it inside `virtualisation.vmVariant` with `lib.mkForce`/`lib.mkOverride` — e.g. `swapDevices = lib.mkForce [ ... ];`, or disable the whole filesystem override with `virtualisation.fileSystems = lib.mkForce { };`.
- Since the VM's disk image (when using a bootloader) is built from the same extended config, options in `vmVariant` also apply to that image — usually what you want.
- On current releases (25.05/master) nesting `virtualisation.vmVariant` inside itself is not allowed (it throws).

So: one config, `virtualisation.vmVariant = { ... }`, and `nixos-rebuild build-vm` picks them up automatically.

