{"answer":"You don't need `allowUnfree = true` (which admits everything). There are two options for a narrow allowlist:

**On current nixpkgs (unstable / 25.11-generation) — simplest:**

```nix
{
  nixpkgs.config.allowUnfreePackages = [ "steam" "nvidia-x11" ];
}
```

`nixpkgs.config.allowUnfreePackages` is a list of package names that are allowed to be unfree. Per its definition in `pkgs/top-level/config.nix`, it "merges additively, similar to `environment.systemPackages`", so you can declare entries in several modules without centralizing them.

**On any nixpkgs release (incl. 25.05, 24.11) — the classic form:**

```nix
{
  nixpkgs.config.allowUnfreePredicate =
    pkg: builtins.elem (pkg.pname) [ "steam" "nvidia-x11" ];
}
```

The predicate receives each package and returns true for the ones you want to keep. If you also use versioned variants (e.g. `nvidia-x11-550`), a prefix match is more flexible: `pkg: any (p: hasPrefix p pkg.pname) [ "steam" "nvidia-x11" ]`.

**Why this works (checked in source, NixOS/nixpkgs @ master):**

- `pkgs/top-level/config.nix` defines `allowUnfree` (default `false`) and `allowUnfreePackages` (default `[]`, "Allows specific unfree packages to be used. This option composes with `nixpkgs.config.allowUnfreePredicate`").
