{"answer":"## How gen library tests are laid out

Each gen library is its own repository (`sini/gen-<name>`, e.g. `sini/gen-prelude`), and the tests do **not** live in the root flake:

- The **root `flake.nix` of a member library exposes only `lib`** — no `checks` output. gen-prelude's root flake is the clearest example; it declares zero inputs and one comment: *"The test runner lives in ./ci, which is a separate flake."*
- The test suite is a **separate flake at `ci/`** (own `flake.nix`, own `flake.lock`) built from `gen-harness.lib.mkCi`:

  ```nix
  # gen-prelude/ci/flake.nix
  gen-harness.lib.mkCi {
    inherit inputs;
    name = "gen-prelude";
    testModules = ./tests;
    specialArgs = { inherit genPrelude; };
  };
  ```

  `mkCi` (gen-harness `mkCi.nix`) `import`s the whole `ci/tests/` directory via import-tree, so **a new test file becomes a gate the moment it lands — no registration step**. Cells are nix-unit tests: `{ suite-name.test-name = { expr; expected; } }`, with an abortable second plane `flake.testsError`.

## Running them locally

From the **library's own repo root**:

- `nix develop ./ci --command ci` — the canonical local gate. Per the harness's `flakeModule.nix`, it:
  1. runs the **read-roots guard** first (`<name>-ci-read-roots`), which refuses if there is any *untracked* file under a declared read root (`ci/tests/`, declared roots, `examples/`) — the remedy is `git add` or move;
  2. runs the whole suite: `nix-unit --flake $FLAKE_ROOT/ci#tests`;
  3. then builds **every declared `ci#checks.<system>.*` one at a time** (except `tests-error`), so every failing check is named.
- Narrower runs: `nix develop ./ci -c ci <suite>` (one suite), `nix develop ./ci -c ci <suite>.<test>` (one test — note it goes through the harness's `testSingletons` view; pointing nix-unit at a bare `#tests.<suite>.<test>` leaf is a group with no test-prefixed child and silently reports `0/0 successful`, a false pass), `nix develop ./ci -c ci --tests-error` (error plane), and the unguarded direct `nix develop ./ci -c nix-unit --flake ./ci#tests[.suite]`.
- Every member repo also has a GitHub Actions workflow running this on push/PR.

## Why `nix flake check` at the repo root is not enough

1. **The root flake has no `checks`.** `nix flake check` at a member's root only proves the flake *evaluates* (i.e. `lib` computes). It runs **zero tests** — the suite is in the separate `./ci` flake, and `nix flake check` does not recurse into sub-flakes.
2. **Even `nix flake check ./ci` is unguarded.** A flake reads a **git-filtered copy** of the tree, so an *untracked* (not `git add`ed) test file under `ci/tests/` is silently absent — the gate passes green without having run your new test. Only the `ci` devshell command runs the read-roots guard over the real worktree and refuses on untracked files. The hub README states this explicitly: *"The bare `nix flake check ./ci` also runs it but is unguarded, blind to an untracked cell, because it reads a git-filtered copy of the tree."*
3. **The error plane is a separate route.** Cells that can abort live on `flake.testsError` and run via the nix-unit runner (`ci --tests-error` / the workflow's `nix develop --command nix-unit --flake .#testsError` step); gen-merge's own `ci.yml` comment says *"nix flake check covers the tests output ONLY … the error-assertion cells live on testsError, so without this step they never run here."*
4. **If you mean the hub (`sini/gen`) itself:** it is an aggregator — it "owns no concern of its own", and the unit tests of its 23 members are in *their* repos, not in the hub. The hub's root flake also declares no `checks`; its own gates are the separate `ci/` flake (parity oracle via `nix flake check ./ci`, `mkgenlibs-eval`, `direction-of-dependence`, pin coherence) plus `nix run ./ci#perf-bench` — those test the hub's *pins and roster*, not a library's suite.

**Verified from source:** `sini/gen-prelude` `flake.nix` + `ci/flake.nix`, `sini/gen-harness` `flake.nix`, `mkCi.nix`, `flakeModule.nix` (the `ci` command and `checks.default` asserter), `sini/gen` `flake.nix` (no `checks` output) and README. Not executed: I couldn't run the commands in this sandbox (eval never builds), so the guard's untracked-file refusal and the `0/0` false pass are from the harness source, not a live run; and I checked one member's root flake directly (gen-prelude) with the rest following the same pattern per the hub README.","confidence":0.9,"gaps":["Did not execute `nix develop ./ci --command ci` / `nix flake check ./ci` (eval never builds); guard refusal on untracked files and the 0/0 nix-unit false pass are cited from gen-harness source, not a live run","Verified the root-flake-has-no-checks pattern directly only for gen-prelude; all other members follow it per the hub README's claim that all 23 repos build ci/flake.nix on mkCi","Raw fetch of sini/gen/ci/flake.nix returned 404 once (transient); the file's existence is confirmed by the repo tree page and hub README"],"escalate_forced":"no"}

