**Why `host ? gpu` and not `host.gpu`** — `gpu` is not a den option. The host entity's options, defined in `denful/den` at `nix/lib/entities/host.nix`, are `name`, `hostName`, `system`, `class`, `aspect`, `description`, `users`, `instantiate`, `intoAttr`, `mainModule`, plus the internal `__resolveResult`, `__pathSetByScope`, `resolved`, `__scopeName`, `collisionPolicy` — no `gpu`. And none of the built-in batteries (`modules/aspects/batteries/`, listed in the docs: hostname, define-user, os class, user class, mutual-provider, tty-autologin, vm-autologin, wsl, forward, homeManager/hjem/maid classes, …) define one. The host type is built freeform — `den.hosts` uses `freeformType = deepMergeAttrs` and each host is a gen-schema instance over `den.schema.host` with `freeformType = attrsOf (hostType name)` — so any extra key you write on a host is absorbed into the resolved entity's config.

