{"answer":"**Forward into an existing class when the class is a naming/scoping layer over an existing module system.** If your custom class's config is really NixOS/Darwin/home-manager options that just want a better name, a narrower scope (per-user, per-role, per-platform), a condition, or adapted args — and it doesn't need its own output — forward it with `den.batteries.forward`: it moves the class's content into a target path on an existing class; no separate evaluation happens.

