fwd = { host, user }: den.batteries.forward {
  each = lib.singleton user;
  fromClass  = _: "container";
  intoClass  = _: host.class;
  intoPath   = _: [ "virtualisation" "oci-containers" "containers" user.userName ];
  fromAspect = _: user.aspect;
  # optional: guard = { options, ... }: options ? wsl;
  #            adaptArgs = args: { osConfig = args.config; };
};
```

This is exactly how den implements the `user` class (→ `users.users.<name>`), `homeManager` (→ `home-manager.users.<name>`), `hjem`, `maid`, the built-in `os` class, and community examples like `hm` aliases, platform-specific hm classes, role classes, and guarded forwards. A fixed destination can be declared once on the class (`den.classes.custom = { forwardTo = { class = "nixos"; path = [ ]; }; }` so forwards only name the source); at the lower level the same move is a `den.lib.policy.route` policy — den's own `os`/`user`/`wsl` classes use `route`, while `homeManager`/`hjem`/`maid` use `forward`.

