{"answer":"**Why it happens:** each `den.homes.<name>` emits its own definition of the `flake.homeConfigurations` output, and den (like flake-parts) deliberately does not declare an option with merge semantics for flake output attributes — the module system therefore can't merge the second definition and fails with "defined multiple times while it's expected to be unique". This is den discussion #317 (converted from issue #315), which is exactly this error.

**The fix (current den, ≥ v0.14.0; latest is v0.19.0):** den now ships ready-made option-declaration modules under `inputs.den.flakeOutputs`. Import the one for your output at the top level of your module tree:

```nix
# in your top-level/root module (the one that feeds all your modules)
{ inputs, ... }:
{
  imports = [ inputs.den.flakeOutputs.homeConfigurations ];
}
```

That declares `options.flake.homeConfigurations` as a `lazyAttrsOf` freeform submodule, so the per-home definitions merge. If you also have multiple hosts, import `inputs.den.flakeOutputs.all` instead — it declares mergeable options for `nixosConfigurations`, `darwinConfigurations`, `homeConfigurations` plus the per-system outputs (`packages`, `checks`, `apps`, `tests`, `devShells`, `legacyPackages`). The error message shipped in den points you to exactly this import.

**If you're on an older den (< v0.14.0), or want to own the merge strategy yourself:** define the option in your own module:

```nix
{ lib, ... }:
{
  options.flake.homeConfigurations = lib.mkOption {
    default = { };
    type = lib.types.lazyAttrsOf lib.types.raw;
  };
}
```

This is the fix the maintainer gave in #317; it applies with or without flake-parts (flake-parts has the same gap, since it also doesn't declare these options).

**How I know:** I read `nix/flakeOutputs.nix` on `denful/den` main — the file's own comment links to discussion #317, and it defines `flakeBased` (with `homeConfigurations`), `systemBased`, `all`, and `flake`, with an embedded error message telling users to `imports = [ inputs.den.flakeOutputs.nixosConfigurations ]`-style imports or declare their own `options.flake.<name>`. `nix/default.nix` exports it as `flakeOutputs`, and the v0.14.0 release notes confirm the mechanism landed in PR #319 ("better error message on non-mergable flake outputs"), right after that discussion.","confidence":0.85,"gaps":["eval and clone were unavailable in this environment, so I could not byte-verify nix/flakeOutputs.nix at the v0.19.0 tag (I read it from main and cross-checked against v0.14.0 release notes/PR #319)","asker's exact den rev unknown; if < v0.14.0 the flakeOutputs import does not exist and the manual option definition is required"],"escalate_forced":"no"}

